Feature: GPU flag "draw_every_nth_frame" (the emulated GPU draws only every Nth frame)

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk),
            AFTER 0004 and 0009 (its draw check extends 0009's skip_draws line)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0013-draw-every-nth-frame.patch
Status:     local patch (a feature for our port, not a bug fix)

WHY
  Dual mode runs both renderers: the emulated picture in the main window,
  our native one in a second window. Both draw every frame on one host GPU.
  Measured 2026-10-03 (Ice Prison save, standing still, 60 fps cap): GPU
  94% busy for the emulated picture alone, 97% in dual mode. 60 fps held
  there, but busier scenes (fights, effects) dropped frames, which made
  side-by-side testing painful. Lowering the emulated GPU's quality would
  change the picture we compare against, so instead it draws fewer frames,
  each one complete and exact.

WHAT
  A hot-reloadable int flag draw_every_nth_frame (default 1 = unchanged,
  range 1-4) in the generic command processor. Frames are counted at the
  swap packet (frame_cycle_); frame k is drawn when k % N == 0. In the
  other frames every draw packet (resolves included) is parsed and skipped,
  like 0009's skip_draws, and the Vulkan IssueSwap ends the frame WITHOUT
  presenting it: the game alternates two frontbuffers, so the skipped
  frame's one still holds an older picture, and showing it would make the
  window jump back in time. The window keeps the last drawn frame.
  The flag is read at every draw (CurrentFrameSkipped), not latched per
  frame: the port switches it to 1 at the moment an A/B photo starts (in
  the middle of a frame), and the rest of that frame plus the captured
  next one must be drawn.
  The D3D12 backend is not changed (draws are skipped there too, but its
  swap still presents: not used by the port on Linux).

HOW WE MEASURED IT (2026-10-03)
  Same save and spot, dual mode, 60 fps cap: N = 1 GPU 96-97% busy,
  N = 2 GPU 60% busy, 60.0 fps in both. Same-frame A/B captures
  (--debug_native_ab_ms, three of them) still pair up: 0.53/255 as before.
  Set by the game side (src/native/native_renderer.cpp,
  UpdateEmulatedFrameRate; flag --emulated_draw_every, default 2).

